Any of those combinations will slice and dice their way through the
dungeon with much carnage.  I don't like Frostbrand because it freezes
potions.  My personal preference is to stick with Excalibur and #two-
weapon it with the first silver saber that I find.  It does plenty of
damage and also allows me to start using my Enchant Weapon scrolls
rather than carting them around.  Also altar camping can take a while
so I'd rather just get on with the game, err... that is trying to win,
rather than trying to fully optimize.  But given the choice between
Excalibur and Grayswandir, the choice is definitely Grayswandir
(IMHO).

A drawback is that you won't be able to bribe Asmodeus and Baalzebub.
I think if you drop Excalibur before entering their level then you can
bribe them but I've always entered their level and then they never
offer to go away for a price ... but I'm guessing.

